# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides information about an authentication domain mapping, i.e. the link between a Bastion
user group and the external group of an authentication domain (LDAP, Active Directory, Azure AD
or SAML).

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Look up an existing authentication domain
data "wallix-bastion_authdomain_ad" "corporate" {
  domain_name = "corporate.local"
}

# Get information about the mapping of a specific user group on that domain
data "wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping" "admins" {
  domain_id  = data.wallix-bastion_authdomain_ad.corporate.id
  user_group = "administrators"
}

# Use the mapped external group elsewhere
output "administrators_external_group" {
  value = data.wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping.admins.external_group
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Lookup Keys

This data source requires **both** of the following Required arguments to identify a unique
mapping:

- `domain_id`: The ID of the authentication domain the mapping belongs to (e.g. the `id`
  attribute from a `wallix-bastion_authdomain_ad`, `wallix-bastion_authdomain_ldap`,
  `wallix-bastion_authdomain_azuread`, or `wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml` data source).
- `user_group`: The Bastion user group name the mapping is defined for.

There is no single-field lookup — a mapping is only unique per `(domain_id, user_group)` pair.
The data source fails if no mapping exists for that combination.

### Returned Attributes

- **external_group**: The external directory/IdP group (LDAP DN, Azure AD group name, SAML
  role, etc.) mapped to `user_group` on this domain.
- **domain**: The internal domain reference associated with the mapping.

### Usage in Resources

Combine this data source with the domain-specific data sources
(`wallix-bastion_authdomain_ad`, `wallix-bastion_authdomain_ldap`,
`wallix-bastion_authdomain_azuread`, `wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml`) to look up an existing
mapping's external group without having to manage the mapping as a resource.
